# Denis Architecture (ADR-005 Maximum)

## Before coding

1. Read `docs/architecture/denis-implementation-map.md` — **§3 as-built** and **§4 gaps**
2. North star: `docs/architecture/ADR-005-denis-maximum.md`
3. **M0–M10 complete** — next work is **M11+** unless fixing spine bugs
4. Identify **one M-track** only

## Where code goes

| Layer | Path |
|-------|------|
| Config | `src/lib/denis/config/` |
| Platform / timeline | `src/lib/denis/platform/` |
| Kernel | `src/lib/denis/kernel/` |
| Venue OS | `src/lib/denis/venue/` |
| Runtime PPAN+ | `src/lib/denis/runtime/` |
| Surfaces | `src/lib/denis/surfaces/` |
| Order Core ACL | `src/lib/denis/acl/` |
| Learning | `src/lib/denis/learning/` |
| Eval | `src/lib/denis/eval/` |

**Do not** add new Denis business logic to `src/lib/ai/chat-service.ts` (wrapper only).  
Legacy LLM/ordering stays in `src/lib/ai/execute-chat-turn.ts` until `runtime/narrate/` cutover.

## Invariants

- Only ACL (+ legacy `order-executor.ts`) → Order Core / `create-order`
- T3 narrates facts only — never decides cart/submit
- `denis_timeline` append-only
- No module-level `Map`/`Set` in `src/lib/denis/`
- OpenAI in `denis/` only under `runtime/narrate/` and `runtime/perceive/` (future)
- One PR = one M-track

## Before finish

```bash
pnpm verify:denis
pnpm eval:denis    # if kernel/planner/runtime planning touched
pnpm type-check
```

Fix all compliance **errors** before commit.
